1
00:00:04,750 --> 00:00:06,710
Hey! I'm all packed and ready to go.

2
00:00:08,090 --> 00:00:11,590
Oh, that's right. Daddy and Uncle Joey are going on a trip today.

3
00:00:11,760 --> 00:00:14,130
We're going to a conference in Barbados. Right?

4
00:00:14,300 --> 00:00:16,680
Uh-huh.

5
00:00:14,300 --> 00:00:16,680
Can you say, "Barbados"?

6
00:00:16,850 --> 00:00:18,510
Barbados.

7
00:00:20,560 --> 00:00:24,730
Okay. I've gotta say, it means so much to me that you guys are coming...

8
00:00:24,890 --> 00:00:27,400
all the way over there to hear me give my speech.

9
00:00:27,560 --> 00:00:30,400
Ooh, and I have a surprise. I had to pull some strings...

10
00:00:30,570 --> 00:00:35,700
but I was able to get everyone passes to the entire conference. That's right!

11
00:00:37,450 --> 00:00:42,330
These babies will get you into all the paleontology lectures and seminars.

12
00:00:42,950 --> 00:00:46,620
Do you have anything that will get us out of them?

13
00:00:47,540 --> 00:00:50,460
We're excited to hear the speech, but the rest of the time...

14
00:00:50,630 --> 00:00:52,670
we're gonna want to do island stuff.

15
00:00:52,840 --> 00:00:55,050
David'll probably want to hear a few lectures.

16
00:00:55,220 --> 00:00:57,260
Right, because he's a scientist.

17
00:00:55,220 --> 00:00:57,260
No, no.

18
00:00:57,430 --> 00:01:01,100
He's been in Minsk for eight years. If he gets too much direct sunlight...

19
00:01:01,260 --> 00:01:03,060
he'll die.

20
00:01:03,560 --> 00:01:05,350
Okay, we'd better go.

21
00:01:03,560 --> 00:01:05,350
Yeah?

22
00:01:05,520 --> 00:01:08,270
So we'll see you guys tomorrow.

23
00:01:05,520 --> 00:01:08,270
All right, let's do it.

24
00:01:08,440 --> 00:01:11,110
A five-hour flight with Charlie, have a couple drinks...

25
00:01:11,270 --> 00:01:13,730
get under that blanket and do what comes natural.

26
00:01:13,900 --> 00:01:17,110
It's a blanket, Joe, not a cloak of invisibility.

27
00:02:14,050 --> 00:02:20,680
Wow, this place is beautiful!

28
00:02:14,050 --> 00:02:20,680
Look at all these paleontologists!

29
00:02:20,840 --> 00:02:25,060
I know. There are gonna be some pasty folks by the pool tomorrow.

30
00:02:25,640 --> 00:02:27,930
Oh, my God, I can't believe you're here!

31
00:02:28,140 --> 00:02:29,310
I think I've been recognized.

32
00:02:29,480 --> 00:02:33,860
This happens all the time.

33
00:02:29,480 --> 00:02:33,860
Dr. Geller? I am such a huge fan.

34
00:02:34,020 --> 00:02:36,440
That never happens.

35
00:02:36,610 --> 00:02:41,030
I've been following your career for years. I can't wait for your keynote speech.

36
00:02:41,870 --> 00:02:45,820
Wow. This is very flattering...

37
00:02:41,870 --> 00:02:45,820
I would love your autograph.

38
00:02:46,040 --> 00:02:49,830
Well, sure. Um...

39
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:51,040
Dear?

40
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:51,040
Sarah.

41
00:02:51,210 --> 00:02:55,340
Sarah. I dig you.

42
00:02:57,260 --> 00:03:00,470
Dr. Ross Geller.

43
00:02:57,260 --> 00:03:00,470
Oh, thank you so much.

44
00:03:00,630 --> 00:03:04,970
Sure. Sarah, I'd like you to introduce you to my colleague, Professor Wheeler.

45
00:03:06,390 --> 00:03:09,180
And this is Joey Tribbiani.

46
00:03:06,390 --> 00:03:09,180
Are you a paleontologist?

47
00:03:09,390 --> 00:03:12,940
No, God, no, no. I'm an actor.

48
00:03:13,100 --> 00:03:16,690
You probably recognize me from a little show called The Days of Our Lives.

49
00:03:16,860 --> 00:03:21,570
Dude, it's just Days of Our Lives. There's no "the."

50
00:03:23,740 --> 00:03:30,040
Okay, Ross, boy, you... Yeah. No, no. I play Dr. Drake Ramoray.

51
00:03:30,210 --> 00:03:35,420
I'm sorry. I don't own a TV.

52
00:03:30,210 --> 00:03:35,420
You don't own a TV?

53
00:03:35,590 --> 00:03:37,960
What's all your furniture pointed at?

54
00:03:42,130 --> 00:03:43,340
David, can you help me?

55
00:03:43,510 --> 00:03:47,010
I'm trying to explain to Chandler how a plane stays in the air.

56
00:03:47,180 --> 00:03:50,020
Oh, certainly. That's a combination of Bernoulli's Principle...

57
00:03:50,180 --> 00:03:53,730
and Newton's third law of motion.

58
00:03:50,180 --> 00:03:53,730
See?

59
00:03:53,900 --> 00:03:57,360
Yeah. That's the same as, "It has something to do with wind."

60
00:03:57,860 --> 00:04:00,110
I'm gonna go pick up a few things for the trip.

61
00:04:00,280 --> 00:04:04,860
I should go too. Now, tomorrow do you want to share a cab to the airport...

62
00:04:05,030 --> 00:04:06,660
or should Mike and I meet you?

63
00:04:09,990 --> 00:04:13,040
Mike? Who's Mike?

64
00:04:14,080 --> 00:04:17,500
Mike's your ex

65
00:04:14,080 --> 00:04:17,500
boyfriend.

66
00:04:14,080 --> 00:04:17,500
That's right!

67
00:04:17,670 --> 00:04:20,840
Oh, yeah. Wow, I had totally forgotten about him.

68
00:04:21,010 --> 00:04:27,300
That's a blast from the past, huh?

69
00:04:21,010 --> 00:04:27,300
No, it's okay. Honest mistake.

70
00:04:27,470 --> 00:04:30,470
It really doesn't mean anything. I mean, you know...

71
00:04:30,640 --> 00:04:33,430
Monica refers to Chandler as Richard all the time.

72
00:04:35,900 --> 00:04:38,610
She does?

73
00:04:35,900 --> 00:04:38,610
Let's get you out of here.

74
00:04:44,110 --> 00:04:46,070
Well, at least you took me down with you.

75
00:04:46,870 --> 00:04:50,400
I'm so sorry. I just... I keep thinking about Mike.

76
00:04:50,620 --> 00:04:54,660
I'm crazy about David, and we're having so much fun together.

77
00:04:54,830 --> 00:04:58,710
Why? Why do I miss Mike? That's just... That's gonna go away, right?

78
00:04:58,880 --> 00:05:01,210
Well, I guess. In time.

79
00:04:58,880 --> 00:05:01,210
Yeah.

80
00:05:01,380 --> 00:05:04,050
I mean, my feelings for Richard are certainly gone.

81
00:05:04,220 --> 00:05:09,510
You just did it again. Chandler. Your feelings for Chandler are certainly gone.

82
00:05:11,560 --> 00:05:14,350
Boy, Phoebe's still pretty hung up on that Mike, huh?

83
00:05:14,520 --> 00:05:17,020
I wouldn't read too much into it.

84
00:05:17,980 --> 00:05:20,810
Still, a girl calls you by her ex-boyfriend's name...

85
00:05:20,980 --> 00:05:23,820
that's not a good thing, right?

86
00:05:20,980 --> 00:05:23,820
Let me stop you there.

87
00:05:23,990 --> 00:05:28,530
Because I think I see where this is going. I'm not very good at giving advice.

88
00:05:29,160 --> 00:05:31,990
See, if you want advice, go to Ross or Monica. Or Joey...

89
00:05:32,160 --> 00:05:37,330
for advice about pizza toppings or a burning sensation when you pee.

90
00:05:38,580 --> 00:05:42,630
I'm sorry, I just wish there was something I could do, you know?

91
00:05:43,250 --> 00:05:46,630
Well, you know Phoebe...

92
00:05:43,250 --> 00:05:46,630
Seriously, we're gonna do this?

93
00:05:47,380 --> 00:05:50,760
I'm sorry, I just wish I could make her forget about Mike already.

94
00:05:50,930 --> 00:05:55,770
Why did Phoebe and Mike break up?

95
00:05:50,930 --> 00:05:55,770
Oh, because his penis was too big.

96
00:05:59,100 --> 00:06:02,770
I'm sorry. That's the kind of thing I do.

97
00:06:04,280 --> 00:06:06,860
They broke up because Mike didn't want to get married.

98
00:06:07,030 --> 00:06:09,950
What if you let Phoebe know you'd be open to marriage?

99
00:06:10,700 --> 00:06:14,450
That's great. That's great. I'll propose to her.

100
00:06:14,620 --> 00:06:15,950
What?

101
00:06:16,120 --> 00:06:18,580
I was probably going to do it at some point.

102
00:06:18,750 --> 00:06:21,710
No, I didn't mean now.

103
00:06:18,750 --> 00:06:21,710
Well, why not? It's brilliant.

104
00:06:21,880 --> 00:06:25,000
Goodbye, Mike. We'll see you at the wedding, fella.

105
00:06:25,170 --> 00:06:27,840
Well, we probably won't invite you to the wedding, but..."

106
00:06:28,010 --> 00:06:31,390
Well, thank you, Chandler. Sincerely.

107
00:06:28,010 --> 00:06:31,390
Well, you're welcome.

108
00:06:31,550 --> 00:06:33,180
Glad I could help.

109
00:06:34,890 --> 00:06:38,020
How do you think I should propose?

110
00:06:34,890 --> 00:06:38,020
I'm pretending to read here.

111
00:06:38,180 --> 00:06:39,770
I'm sorry.

112
00:06:43,650 --> 00:06:46,190
Yeah. How you doing?

113
00:06:47,490 --> 00:06:48,650
Hey, hey.

114
00:06:47,490 --> 00:06:48,650
Hey.

115
00:06:48,820 --> 00:06:51,490
You said you were gonna wear a thong. Where's the thong?

116
00:06:52,370 --> 00:06:57,030
Ha, ha, I didn't mean a thong. I meant thongs.

117
00:06:58,290 --> 00:07:00,660
You really should have been more clear about that.

118
00:07:05,040 --> 00:07:07,800
You're never gonna guess who I just saw downstairs.

119
00:07:08,720 --> 00:07:10,550
Oh, uh, uh, Britney Spears!

120
00:07:10,760 --> 00:07:13,720
Yeah. She never misses these conferences.

121
00:07:14,220 --> 00:07:17,680
No, I just saw Dr. Kenneth Schwartz!

122
00:07:14,220 --> 00:07:17,680
Oh, my God!

123
00:07:17,850 --> 00:07:19,980
I know!

124
00:07:17,850 --> 00:07:19,980
Did you talk to him?

125
00:07:20,140 --> 00:07:22,810
Oh, yeah. What am I gonna say to Kenneth Schwartz?

126
00:07:22,980 --> 00:07:26,900
You could say, "Hey, Kenny, how come you're not Britney Spears?"

127
00:07:27,530 --> 00:07:30,240
You ready to go?

128
00:07:27,530 --> 00:07:30,240
You're gonna go now?

129
00:07:30,400 --> 00:07:34,200
I thought we could hang out.

130
00:07:30,400 --> 00:07:34,200
I can't. I have seminars all day.

131
00:07:34,370 --> 00:07:36,280
I promised Ross I'd look at his speech.

132
00:07:36,950 --> 00:07:42,500
But maybe we could have dinner later? Out on the balcony? Lt'll be romantic.

133
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:44,330
Will you wear a thong?

134
00:07:45,380 --> 00:07:46,790
I will if you will.

135
00:07:47,800 --> 00:07:51,170
You got yourself a very weird deal.

136
00:07:53,590 --> 00:07:55,840
I'm good. I have dinner plans.

137
00:07:57,390 --> 00:07:59,600
So you gonna be okay?

138
00:07:57,390 --> 00:07:59,600
Yeah, yeah.

139
00:07:59,770 --> 00:08:03,640
I got tons of stuff I could do. I'm gonna hit the beach, go swimming.

140
00:08:03,810 --> 00:08:05,560
Joe, have you looked outside?

141
00:08:06,560 --> 00:08:08,150
No. Why?

142
00:08:11,030 --> 00:08:13,450
Oh, man.

143
00:08:11,030 --> 00:08:13,450
There's an indoor pool.

144
00:08:13,610 --> 00:08:14,950
You could swim there.

145
00:08:13,610 --> 00:08:14,950
Yeah.

146
00:08:15,110 --> 00:08:18,740
I wasn't gonna swim. I was gonna dig a hole.

147
00:08:23,580 --> 00:08:26,670
That "Mike" was interesting. I don't know what's gonna happen...

148
00:08:26,830 --> 00:08:31,420
with Phoebe and David.

149
00:08:26,830 --> 00:08:31,420
I do. Want a hint, huh?

150
00:08:31,710 --> 00:08:36,640
I do. I do.

151
00:08:37,220 --> 00:08:40,060
Okay, I'm sensing this is some kind of wordplay...

152
00:08:40,220 --> 00:08:43,180
because you are pink with barely controlled glee.

153
00:08:44,020 --> 00:08:48,400
David's gonna propose to Phoebe.

154
00:08:44,020 --> 00:08:48,400
What? Why?

155
00:08:49,150 --> 00:08:51,900
Because we were talking about ways he could beat Mike...

156
00:08:52,070 --> 00:08:54,400
and I told him Phoebe wanted to get married.

157
00:08:54,570 --> 00:08:56,950
Chandler, we have talked about this.

158
00:08:57,110 --> 00:08:59,870
You are not supposed to give people advice!

159
00:09:01,540 --> 00:09:04,200
Couldn't you have made some inappropriate joke?

160
00:09:04,370 --> 00:09:06,500
I did! A penis one!

161
00:09:07,170 --> 00:09:09,750
Just so I know, what was so wrong about what I said?

162
00:09:09,920 --> 00:09:12,000
They've only been going out for a few weeks.

163
00:09:12,170 --> 00:09:16,550
Phoebe is completely hung up on Mike. I mean, she'll say no...

164
00:09:16,720 --> 00:09:20,220
David's heart will be broken, it'll be too hard for them to recover...

165
00:09:20,390 --> 00:09:23,390
and then Phoebe will end up alone again.

166
00:09:24,140 --> 00:09:26,350
Man, that's some bad advice.

167
00:09:33,650 --> 00:09:36,360
Oh, hey. Thank God. You guys are here.

168
00:09:36,530 --> 00:09:40,070
What's going on?

169
00:09:36,530 --> 00:09:40,070
Everything is upside

170
00:09:36,530 --> 00:09:40,070
down here.

171
00:09:40,240 --> 00:09:45,870
It rains all day long and nobody watches TV, and Ross is famous.

172
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:49,620
I don't want to alarm anybody...

173
00:09:49,790 --> 00:09:53,300
but Monica's hair is twice as big as it was when we landed.

174
00:09:54,130 --> 00:09:56,590
Okay. When I go places with high humidity...

175
00:09:56,760 --> 00:10:00,010
it gets a little extra body, okay?

176
00:10:00,390 --> 00:10:04,180
That's why our honeymoon photos look like me and Diana Ross.

177
00:10:04,640 --> 00:10:06,470
I'll show you guys where to check in.

178
00:10:06,640 --> 00:10:09,730
Oh, honey? Can you make sure we get a king-size bed?

179
00:10:09,900 --> 00:10:14,440
Oh, David, get one for us too. Oh, and see if they have a heart-shaped one.

180
00:10:14,610 --> 00:10:17,490
And with mirrors on the ceiling.

181
00:10:18,030 --> 00:10:21,410
And make sure our room isn't next to theirs.

182
00:10:21,570 --> 00:10:24,990
Oh, you guys are so lucky you're here with people.

183
00:10:25,200 --> 00:10:27,200
You know, it's just such a romantic place.

184
00:10:27,370 --> 00:10:32,000
I just wish I could share it with a guy.

185
00:10:33,840 --> 00:10:36,250
Not Joey.

186
00:10:33,840 --> 00:10:36,250
Not Joey. No.

187
00:10:36,420 --> 00:10:41,260
I was just lusting after Chandler.

188
00:10:36,420 --> 00:10:41,260
Yeah, right.

189
00:10:44,010 --> 00:10:48,350
So I'm proposing to Phoebe tonight.

190
00:10:48,520 --> 00:10:50,230
Tonight?

191
00:10:50,480 --> 00:10:53,610
Isn't an engagement ring supposed to have a diamond?

192
00:10:54,770 --> 00:10:56,820
Oh, there it is.

193
00:10:57,610 --> 00:10:59,530
Yes, well, being a failed scientist...

194
00:10:59,700 --> 00:11:01,950
doesn't pay quite as well as you might think.

195
00:11:02,110 --> 00:11:05,530
That's one-seventieth of a carat.

196
00:11:05,700 --> 00:11:09,250
And the clarity is quite poor.

197
00:11:11,080 --> 00:11:12,670
Nice.

198
00:11:14,340 --> 00:11:17,250
Monica, can I talk to you for a second?

199
00:11:14,340 --> 00:11:17,250
Okay.

200
00:11:17,420 --> 00:11:19,300
David's gonna propose to Phoebe tonight.

201
00:11:19,470 --> 00:11:22,510
See what happens when you give people advice?

202
00:11:23,010 --> 00:11:26,180
Well, I hope you told him not to.

203
00:11:23,010 --> 00:11:26,180
That would be advice!

204
00:11:27,140 --> 00:11:29,270
Okay, fine. I'll handle this.

205
00:11:32,140 --> 00:11:33,900
Phoebe?

206
00:11:32,140 --> 00:11:33,900
Yeah?

207
00:11:34,650 --> 00:11:38,570
I need to talk to you.

208
00:11:34,650 --> 00:11:38,570
Are you leaving the Supremes?

209
00:11:44,910 --> 00:11:50,370
Okay, my husband just gave your boyfriend some very bad advice.

210
00:11:50,540 --> 00:11:52,620
David's gonna propose to you tonight.

211
00:11:53,210 --> 00:11:55,460
Wow, really?

212
00:11:56,340 --> 00:11:58,380
That's fantastic!

213
00:11:59,420 --> 00:12:02,260
What? Are you serious? You want to marry him?

214
00:12:02,430 --> 00:12:05,510
What about Mike?

215
00:12:02,430 --> 00:12:05,510
Oh, okay, you want me to marry Mike?

216
00:12:05,680 --> 00:12:07,890
Let's just gag him and handcuff him...

217
00:12:08,060 --> 00:12:10,390
...and force him down the aisle, okay?

218
00:12:10,560 --> 00:12:12,890
I can just see it. "Mike, do you take Phoebe?"

219
00:12:15,940 --> 00:12:19,230
You know? It's every girl's dream.

220
00:12:19,900 --> 00:12:22,900
Do you really think marrying someone else is the right answer?

221
00:12:23,070 --> 00:12:27,370
Sure. Look, okay, bottom line? I love Mike... David!

222
00:12:28,410 --> 00:12:31,410
David! I love David.

223
00:12:31,580 --> 00:12:34,330
Don't look at me that way, Roseanne Roseannadanna.

224
00:12:38,420 --> 00:12:43,420
By using CT scans and computer imaging, we can, in a very real way…

225
00:12:43,590 --> 00:12:48,470
bring the Mesozoic Era into the 21st century."

226
00:12:50,140 --> 00:12:51,510
It's great.

227
00:12:51,680 --> 00:12:53,520
You'll be the hit of the conference.

228
00:12:53,680 --> 00:12:55,230
It'll be even better tomorrow...

229
00:12:55,390 --> 00:12:58,020
because I won't be constantly interrupted by Joey...

230
00:12:58,190 --> 00:13:01,150
checking to see if they put chocolates on my pillow yet.

231
00:13:05,490 --> 00:13:07,360
Hey, guys.

232
00:13:05,490 --> 00:13:07,360
The chocolates aren't here.

233
00:13:07,530 --> 00:13:09,570
Damn it!

234
00:13:09,740 --> 00:13:12,080
Ross just read me his speech. It's fantastic.

235
00:13:12,240 --> 00:13:15,750
Oh, is it on the computer? Because I'd love to give it a read.

236
00:13:15,920 --> 00:13:19,040
If you want to check your e-mail, just ask.

237
00:13:19,210 --> 00:13:21,040
What? May I?

238
00:13:23,710 --> 00:13:28,930
What's with the rain, Geller? I mean, when I signed up for dino week...

239
00:13:29,090 --> 00:13:31,760
nobody said anything about it being monsoon season.

240
00:13:31,930 --> 00:13:35,980
The wet season is June to December.

241
00:13:31,930 --> 00:13:35,980
It's not the time, Charlie.

242
00:13:36,140 --> 00:13:37,940
Oh, no. No, no! Dear God, no!

243
00:13:38,100 --> 00:13:41,150
What, did someone outbid you for the teapot?

244
00:13:43,780 --> 00:13:46,490
Secret teapot.

245
00:13:46,780 --> 00:13:49,280
Your computer. I don't know what... Everything's gone.

246
00:13:49,450 --> 00:13:51,370
What do you mean?

247
00:13:49,450 --> 00:13:51,370
Must be a virus.

248
00:13:51,530 --> 00:13:53,790
I think it erased your hard drive.

249
00:13:53,950 --> 00:13:56,500
What? Oh, my God. What did you do?

250
00:13:56,660 --> 00:13:59,420
Someone I don't know sent me an e-mail and I opened it.

251
00:13:59,580 --> 00:14:03,670
Why? Why would you open it?

252
00:13:59,580 --> 00:14:03,670
Well, it didn't say, "This is a virus."

253
00:14:03,960 --> 00:14:06,460
What did it say?

254
00:14:03,960 --> 00:14:06,460
Nude...

255
00:14:08,930 --> 00:14:10,590
Pictures of Anna Kournikova.

256
00:14:11,970 --> 00:14:14,100
I'm so sorry.

257
00:14:11,970 --> 00:14:14,100
What am I gonna do?

258
00:14:14,270 --> 00:14:16,720
